#: include/global_form.php
msgid "For SNMPv2 and SNMPv3 Devices, the SNMP Bulk Walk max-repetitions size. The default is to 'Auto Detect on Re-Index'. For very large switches, high performance servers, Jumbo Frame Networks or for high latency WAN connections, increasing this value may increase poller performance. More data is packed into a single SNMP packet which can reduce data query run time. However, some devices may completely refuse to respond to packets with a max-repetition size which is set too large. This can be especially true for lower-powered IoT type devices or smaller embedded IT appliances. Special attention to the overall network path MTU should also be considered since setting a value which is too high could lead to packet fragmentation."
msgstr "Ku bikoresho bya SNMPv2 na SNMPv3, ingano ntarengwa y'isubiramo rya SNMP Bulk Walk (max-repetitions). Igenamiterere risanzwe ni 'Gushakisha ku buryo bwikora mu ibarura rishya'. Kuri za switch nini cyane, seriveri zikora ku muvuduko mwinshi, imiyoboro ya Jumbo Frame cyangwa imiyoboro ya WAN itinda gusubiza, kongera iyi mibare bishobora kongera imikorere ya poller. Amakuru menshi ashyirwa muri paketi imwe ya SNMP bigabanya igihe ikibazo cy'amakuru kimara gikora. Ariko kandi, ibikoresho bimwe na bimwe bishobora kwanga burundu gusubiza paketi zifite umubare munini cyane w'isubiramo. Ibi bikunze kugaragara cyane ku bikoresho bya IoT bikoresha ingufu nke cyangwa ibikoresho bito bya IT byubatsemo imbere. Hakwiye kandi kwitabwaho ingano ya MTU y'inzira yose y'urusobe kuko gushyiraho igipimo kiri hejuru cyane bishobora gutera icikagurika rya paketi."

